    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.44,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.2,
    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot and scaled each reading back up by its dilution factor. The undiluted reading was 0.42, and the late-hour plateau averaged about 0.425. The 10-fold dilution gave 0.0432, which scales to 0.43. The 3-fold dilution gave 0.154, which scales to 0.46. The 2-fold dilution gave 0.227, which scales to 0.45. If the reader were saturating, the dilution-corrected values would sit well above the undiluted reading and rise as dilution increased. They sit only about 5% above it, which is within a couple of standard deviations of replicate noise (about ±0.005 absolute per read). The plateau from about 6 h onward therefore looks like real stationary phase, not reader saturation. Any underestimate is small, at most roughly 5%."
  },
